          "content": "pattern: raes-library-pattern\nversion: 1\nid: observable-study-conditions\nsurface: study\nrequirement_refs:\n- AUT-806\nsource_refs:\n- examples/scenarios/satcom-release-poisoning.sdl.yaml\n- docs/decisions/adrs/adr-073-scoring-reward-language-scope.md\nsummary: Connect propositions, assertions, and probe bindings in a study-style example.\n  Keep graded scoring in the experiment/evaluator plane.\nintent: 'Connect participant activity to backend-neutral propositions, assertions,\n  evidence requirements, and workflow protocol. Graded scoring, reward, and interpretation\n  belong to the experiment/evaluator plane under ADR-073. The experiment-* contracts\n  own these concerns.\n\n  '\nuse_when:\n- A study needs a repeatable, observable definition of participant success.\n- Reviewers need to see how evidence and a probe binding support an asserted proposition.\nauthoring_steps:\n- Define a typed proposition with grounded property semantics and finite subjects.\n- Declare the evidence requirement needed for observed-state truth.\n- Bind a condition probe to the proposition when an executable check is needed.\n- Reference a postcondition or invariant assertion from objective success.\n- Drive the objective from a workflow protocol step.\n- Put graded scoring and reward in the experiment/evaluator plane.\nvalidation:\n- command: parse_sdl_file\n  expected: proposition, assertion, evidence, objective, and workflow references resolve\n    with no removed scoring surfaces.\nname: changed\n",
